From e1d37fab6ce977c24d890aee2b76bee1b6abd0eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:34:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(gateway): in-process Bot Chat follows profile;
 intent on physical target

- session_ingress/session_local_profile: an unmanaged (desktop, in-process) following session
  commits its turn's effective selection before _handle_message and holds that SAME profile read
  for the turn's policy_scope (one read for commit + build); a held pick's end republishes the
  released receipt for the turn.
- session_profile_selection: the switch intent names local_physical_target (what the in-process
  build and reserve_admission_worker use after compression), not the logical id. The remembered
  selection includes the physical target and the receipt's frozen pick, so compaction or an
  explicit pick consumed by another build (cold /review) re-arms it; an unchanged rebuild doesn't.
  Returns the published policy.
- tests/gateway/test_bot_chat_follow_entry.py: real submit->drain->execute_admission (flat and
  compressed), one profile read, composer hold end, explicit pick consumed elsewhere, class
  default, managed real admission/reservation after compression, stale epoch/generation/policy,
  prepared mutation racing a hold release.
